# .dockerignore
#
# The build context is deliberately near-empty: the Dockerfile fetches the
# public-pool source itself from a pinned upstream commit, so nothing in this
# repo needs to reach the builder. Excluding everything keeps the context small
# and makes it impossible for a stray local file to end up in the image.

*

# Nothing is un-ignored. If the build ever needs a file from this repo (e.g. a
# patch to apply on top of upstream), add an explicit `!path` exception here.
